course: dictionary
lesson: 16109
title: Old words, changing meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to old times. You can find them in old stories, ballads and plays, and they tell you the story is set long ago. «The serving wench carried hot bread to the tired travellers at the inn.» The words serving and inn are clues: they point to a girl who worked for the people staying there.
explain: Use the context to check. Swap in a word you know: «The serving girl carried hot bread to the tired travellers» still makes sense, so wench means girl here.
explain: Words can change over time. Wench was once a plain word for a girl or young woman, but today it is old-fashioned and often rude when said to a woman. You may meet it in old books and understand it, but you should not use it yourself.
fact: Wench is a noun: a wench, wenches.
fact: «Wench» means a girl or young woman, especially a servant girl or a country girl (an old use).
fact: Today «wench» is old-fashioned and often rude when said to a woman.
fact: Old stories, ballads and plays may use «wench», which tells you the story is set long ago.
fact: Do not call anyone a wench today.
exercise: «The serving wench carried hot bread to the travellers at the inn.» What is a wench in this sentence? | *A servant girl | A knight in shining armour | A bell-ringer | A large wooden table
exercise: «In the old ballad, the wench sang by the well.» Which word in this sentence tells you the story is old? | by | *old | sang | well
exercise: Jess says, «Wench is just a fancy word for girl, so I can call my friend a wench.» What should Jess know? | *Today it is old-fashioned and often rude, so she should not say it | It is a number | It means a horse | It is a kind, modern word, so it is fine
test: «The wench at the inn wiped the tables and poured the ale.» What is a wench here? | A bell-ringer | A loud song | *A servant girl at an inn | A kind of cloth
test: What is the best meaning of «wench» when said to a woman today? | The name of a town | A polite name to be proud of | *Old-fashioned and often rude | A happy way to say hello
exam: Maya says, «A wench is just a girl, so it's fine to call my sister one today.» What is the best answer? | It is fine, it only means girl | *It was once a plain word for girl, but today it is old-fashioned and often rude, so Maya should not say it | It means a type of cake | It means a loud bird
